 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**24 tests fail and 1 errors** (462 pass, 1 skipped).\n\n**Main root cause:** `src/tessel/sessions.py:374` calls `response.set_cookie(..., partitioned=partitioned, ...)`, but the installed Werkzeug's `Response.set_cookie()` doesn't accept a `partitioned` keyword. That gives `TypeError: Response.set_cookie() got an unexpected keyword argument 'partitioned'`. The installed Werkzeug is probably older than the version that added cookie partitioning, so this looks like a version mismatch.\n\nAny test that saves a session cookie hits it. That accounts for about 20 of the 24 failures:\n- 13 session tests in `test_basic.py`, including `test_session_*` and `test_extended_flashing`\n- `test_stream_keeps_session` in `test_helpers.py`\n- `test_copy_context_thread` in `test_reqctx.py`\n- `test_flash_signal` in `test_signals.py`\n- `test_standard_context` in `test_templating.py`\n- 3 tests in `test_testing.py`\n\n**Other failures** (I did not inspect these in detail, so the causes are unconfirmed):\n- `test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`: `RuntimeError`, likely an async-support dependency issue.\n- `test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`: a pytest-level error.\n- `test_reqctx.py::test_session_dynamic_cookie_name` and `test_request.py::test_limit_config`: assertion failures. They may be related to the Werkzeug version, or independent.\n- The 1 error is in `TestStreaming::test_stream_keeps_session` fixture or teardown, tied to the same `TypeError`.\n\nI haven't changed anything.",
